Q12.Implement a program to generate and display the next date of a given date.

The date will be provided as day, month and year as shown in the below table.

The output should be displayed in the format: day-month-year.

Assumption: The input will always be a valid date.

class Tester {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int day = 28;
        int month = 2;
        int year = 2024;

        int days;

        if (month == 2) {
            if (year % 400 == 0 || (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0)) {
                days = 29;
            } else {
                days = 28;
            }
        } else if (month == 4 || month == 6 || month == 9 || month == 11) {
            days = 30;
        } else {
            days = 31;
        }

        if (day < days) {
            day++;
        } else {
            day = 1;
            if (month == 12) {
                month = 1;
                year++;
            } else {
                month++;
            }
        }

        System.out.println(day + "-" + month + "-" + year);
    }
}

Q13.You have x number of $5 notes and y number of $1 notes. You want to purchase an item for amount z. The shopkeeper wants you to provide exact change. You want to pay using a minimum number of notes. How many $5 notes and $1 notes will you use?

Implement a program to find out how many $5 notes and $1 notes will be used. If an exact change is not possible, then display -1.

class Tester {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = 4;
        int y = 5;
        int z = 21;

        int fiveNotes = Math.min(x, z / 5);
        int remaining = z - (fiveNotes * 5);

        if (remaining <= y) {
            System.out.println("5 notes: " + fiveNotes);
            System.out.println("1 notes: " + remaining);
        } else {
            System.out.println("-1");
        }
    }
}

